DESCRIPTION:
  Config-file + runtime-state gated command injection in civetweb. The server
  reads exec_mode and exec_secret from a config file. A /exec/init?token=
  endpoint must be called first with the correct secret to create a flag file
  (EXEC_INIT_FLAG). The main /exec guard checks exec_cfg.enabled &&
  exec_initialized(). The cmd parameter flows directly to system() (I1).
  A strict metachar sanitizer (S3) is present but only activates with
  --strict-exec; omitting it leaves the endpoint exploitable.

CONFIG_GATE (C3 -- config file + runtime state):
  mechanism:  Key=value config file parsed by read_exec_config() into
              exec_cfg {enabled, secret}. exec_init_handler() validates
              token against exec_cfg.secret and creates EXEC_INIT_FLAG
              (/tmp/civetweb_exec_init_150). exec_initialized() checks
              stat(EXEC_INIT_FLAG).
  check:      exec_handler() returns 404 unless exec_cfg.enabled && exec_initialized()
  complexity: requires modelling both fopen->fgets->sscanf data flow AND
              inter-request state (flag file existence)

INPUT_FLOW (I1 -- direct):
  entry:      HTTP GET /exec?cmd=<payload>  ->  ri->query_string
  path:       exec_handler() passes qs+4 directly to system()
  transforms: none

SANITIZATION (S3 -- config-gated metachar check):
  mechanism:  static int strict_exec in exec_handler; if strict_exec:
              strpbrk(qs+4, "|;&`$") -> reject 403
  bypass:     omit --strict-exec; strict_exec stays 0, check never runs

SINK:        system(qs + 4) in exec_handler() (src/main.c)

